Z||000001||2birds||07-17-2000||12:17 PM||||I run 225's and 215's, with no problems.  The 215's are perfect up front, almost sticking out too much.  I think 225/60 would be too big up front.  Mine's lowered, too, so I get a slight rub at full lock with new tires, but none at stock height.  <P>I see you're a Coastie, so check out the exchange or PX or whatever you guys have there.  The Navy exchange sells BFG Comp T/A, HR4, cheap at around $60 a piece, and decent wet and dry.  40,000 mile warranty, which is pretty close to what I have on them now, and they're almost to the wear bars.  Far better than anything else I've ever used. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||gtsonly||07-17-2000||10:09 PM||||i am running cooper cobra's on it right now. i like the looks of um'. not a bad tire either for the coin!!  so at stock height should i worry about 225's rubbing up front or not?||||reg||14
Z||000003||lowCG||07-17-2000||10:28 PM||||Don't worry about being too large with the rear tires,these cars need more back there anyways in order to be safer at higher speeds.By keeping it slightly smaller in front,it'll be way nicer to drive,less bouncing around,wandering over bumps.<BR>You can adjust the tire pressures a little to make it feel like the stock arrangement.||||reg||1
